Well, as for a concrete proposal, I suggest {skientia}. Is it a valid
fu'ivla?

It is imported from Latin "scientia". As previously pointed, Latin plays a
major role in the written tradition that shaped our modern concept of
science, having been once called the language of science. I used the
classical pronunciation, because in New Latin there was too much variation.
Classical is somewhat neutral and plays nice with Lojban {saske}.

mu'o
mi'e .asiz.


